    "title": "Teaching guide",
    "section": "Partner boundaries and equal access",
    "url": "/teaching/ai-solutions/instructor.html#section-3",
    "body": "The partner supplies the need and feedback; the instructor owns assessment. Obtain permission before sharing data, deploying externally, or representing the partner. Use approved or fictional information. If partner access changes, the classroom client follows the same outcomes and criteria.\nThe final artifact can be a document kit, repeatable service, decision aid, or no-code experience. A classmate can be the observed user. Public launch, payment collection, and sales success are not required."
