    "url": "/teaching/ai-solutions/milestone-2.html#main",
    "body": "Explore the lesson here. Canvas holds your check-ins, submissions, feedback, and progress.\nReturn to this lesson\nMilestone 2 · after Unit 5\nFirst usable solution\nA snapshot of the same project record.\nProvide the actual versioned artifact or supervised service kit, its chosen AI capability and operating workflow, three varied bench tests, a brief reviewer access/use check, and a meaningful revision with retest. A document-based service is sufficient when another person can complete the bounded task. A mock-up or demonstration deck alone is not.\nInclude the source card, input/output examples, review criteria, exception handoff, and manual fallback. Identify the permitted input, AI contribution, checked output, and implementation route. A supplied-output route must label its AI step as simulated; do not claim a live model connection or automation. Record assistance honestly. If another person has not attempted the task, show that requirement as pending rather than substituting an invented result.\nMilestone 2 rubricCriterion | Share | Meets the goal | Strong transfer |\nUsable end-to-end task | 35% | A reviewer accesses the actual version and completes the bounded task; any assistance and unresolved limitation are recorded. | An unfamiliar reviewer completes a changed input using clear instructions, and the author explains why the design transfers. |\nGrounded AI use and human control | 25% | The chosen capability fits the task; permitted inputs, the AI output, live or simulated execution, reviewer, source boundary, exception, and fallback are explicit and checkable. | Shows a consequential AI error or limitation and an effective correction without relying on the assistant’s self-confidence. |\nTesting, revision, and retest | 25% | Ordinary, incomplete, and exception cases have expected and actual results; a meaningful defect is revised and retested. | Tests whether the change affects another path and explains residual uncertainty or an alternative cause of failure. |\nOperating clarity and evidence record | 15% | Version, sources, steps, AI capability and contribution, live or simulated execution route, observations, and pending actions are understandable and accurately labeled. | A concise change log lets a second person reconstruct what changed, why, and which evidence supports the current version. |\n\nMissing evidence is not yet demonstrated. Partial or unreliable evidence is developing. Strong work explains a new case or alternative interpretation. A favorable project result is not required; the quality of evidence and judgment matters.\nBefore saving this snapshot\nActual usable files and current source version are available.\nAI and human roles, review, exception, and fallback are visible.\nThree varied bench cases record expected and actual behavior."
