    "url": "/teaching/ai-solutions/milestone-3.html#main",
    "body": "Explore the lesson here. Canvas holds your check-ins, submissions, feedback, and progress.\nReturn to this lesson\nMilestone 3 · after Unit 7\nPilot and learning\nA snapshot of the same project record.\nShow the predeclared pilot question and measures, actual user-task record, defensible comparison, complete effort and quality, meaningful revision, and retest. Keep supplied benchmark figures separate from what happened with your version.\nThe result may support continuation, narrowing, or stopping. Grade quality of evaluation and judgment, not a positive AI result. Include the individual explanation near this milestone; together with the later check, it contributes to the individual component recorded under Milestone 5, not a second grade here.\nMilestone 3 rubricCriterion | Share | Meets the goal | Strong transfer |\nTest design and comparison | 25% | Defines version, user task, permitted inputs, baseline/comparison, quality, full-process timing, and decision rules before observing outcomes. | Addresses order, practice, case differences, or selection effects and explains what the design can and cannot establish. |\nActual observation and quantitative integrity | 30% | Records an actual classroom or partner attempt with assistance, completion, quality, complete effort, units, denominators, and missing values correctly labeled. | Uses an inspectable table/figure to expose an exception or tradeoff hidden by a favorable average and reconciles it with the recommendation. |\nMeaningful revision and retest | 25% | Links a consequential finding to a changed artifact or process and documents an actual retest of the affected path. | Checks transfer to a changed case and an unaffected path, explaining any new limitation rather than only reporting success. |\nInterpretation and next decision | 20% | Separates supplied from observed evidence, states limitations, and gives a proportionate continue/revise/stop decision. | Considers an alternative explanation and identifies the next evidence that would most reduce uncertainty. |\n\nMissing evidence is not yet demonstrated. Partial or unreliable evidence is developing. Strong work explains a new case or alternative interpretation. A favorable project result is not required; the quality of evidence and judgment matters.\nBefore saving this snapshot\nPredeclared pilot card and permission/readiness status are included.\nActual task, access, assistance, completion, and quality are traceable.\nFull-process effort and comparison are reported honestly.\nA meaningful revision and actual retest are documented.\nRecommendation, evidence limits, and individual explanation are prepared.\nReturn to the Finish step →"
